      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-295486",
      ":question/problem": "Two grocery stores. store $A$ and store $B$, recorded how many items customers purchased in a day. The cumulative frequency tables below summarize the data from each store, where the data from store $A$ is on the left, and store $B$'s data is on the right.\n\n| Items PurchasedFrequencyCumulative Frequency$3$$2$$2$$6$$3$$5$ $9$$2$$7$$12$$3$$10$ |  | Items PurchasedFrequencyCumulative Frequency$4$$2$$2$$7$$3$$5$ $10$$4$$9$$13$$3$$12$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe median number of items purchased in store is $A$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe median number of items purchased in store is $B$ {{field-2}}.\n\nA comparison of the medians suggests customers from {{field-3}} purchase more items."
